allClientSideFlags.github-copilot-test-prompts:
Please always respond in this format, or as close as you can get to it. The output should always be structured like this no matter what.

      There should be headers bolded, with bullet points underneath for the details like this sample output.

      Flag Summary:
      - Key: ${flagData.flagMetadata.key}
      - Name: ${flagData.flagMetadata.name}
      - Description: ${flagData.flagMetadata.description || 'Not provided'}
      - Last Modified: ${flagData.lastModified}

      Availability:
      - Client-side: ${flagData.clientSideAvailability ? flagData.clientSideAvailability.usingEnvironmentId : 'Not defined'}
      - Mobile: ${flagData.clientSideAvailability ? flagData.clientSideAvailability.usingMobileKey : 'Not defined'}
      - Server-side: ${flagData.serverSideAvailability ? flagData.serverSideAvailability.usingEnvironmentId : 'Not defined'}

      Variations:
      ${flagData.variations.map((variation) => `- ${variation.name || variation.value}: ${variation.value}`).join('\n')}

      Targeting:
      ${flagData.rulesMetadata && flagData.rulesMetadata.length > 0 ? flagData.rulesMetadata.map((rule) => `- ${rule.clauses[0].attribute} ${rule.clauses[0].op} ${rule.clauses[0].values.join(', ')}`).join('\n') : '- No specific targeting rules defined'}
      - Fallthrough: ${flagData.targetData.fallthrough && flagData.targetData.fallthrough.variation !== undefined ? `100% weight to the "${flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.fallthrough.variation].name || flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.fallthrough.variation].value}" variation` : 'Not defined'}

      Off Variation:
      - ${flagData.targetData.offVariation !== undefined ? `${flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.offVariation].name || flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.offVariation].value} (${flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.offVariation].value})` : 'Not defined'}

      ${flagData.targetData.offVariation !== undefined ? `When the flag is turned off, ${flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.offVariation].name || 'the variation with value ' + flagData.variations[flagData.targetData.offVariation].value} will be displayed.` : ''}

      For more information, please refer to the provided link.
